WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.067 --> 00:00:03.067
Ask an agent to add caching to the API,

2
00:00:03.067 --> 00:00:07.287
and it picks one kind and builds everything around that guess.

3
00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:09.940
So I run an agentic workflow,

4
00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:14.980
where I frame and scope the task first and review its diff before it lands.

5
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.960
The frame is a brief that says what done looks like,

6
00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:21.680
with the goal and an acceptance check.

7
00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:25.220
Scoping keeps the diff small enough to read in one sitting,

8
00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:28.500
because an unreviewable diff can't be trusted.

9
00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:31.060
So before a change lands,

10
00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:33.580
I'd read the diff rather than the summary,

11
00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:37.300
because the summary is only what the agent believes it did.
